+## Spec Change Log
+
+- **2026-08-02, review round 1 (Blind Hunter + Edge Case Hunter, 13 actionable findings):**
+  all classified `patch` and fixed in place (no loopback — no intent gaps,
+  no spec deviations beyond the two semantic refinements noted below).
+  Fixed: form_draft.js missing from .gitignore whitelist (blocker — would
+  not have shipped); node_modules symlink staged (unstaged + excluded);
+  failed Resend send consuming the 10-min cooldown (new
+  clear_last_link_sent.sql, mirrors inbound stamp-clearing); PostHog
+  $pageview leaking the 288-bit resume token (sanitize_properties scrub in
+  the apply snippet); sub-2s resumed submit falling into the
+  fake-confirmation black hole (resume render backdates _form_loaded_at 10s
+  + form.js no longer clobbers it on form-resume); empty-fields PUT wiping
+  drafts (guard on both save + continue-link); continue-link sending a
+  stale-state email when its own upsert fails (aborts before claim); client
+  reading the closed-vacancy 200 as success (body.ok check + saver
+  disables); stage-2 N+1 draft lookups (single prefetch +
+  list_resumable_draft_tokens.sql); erasure confirm canonical carrying the
+  token (now the apply path); upsert resurrecting stripped drafts after a
+  late beacon (ON CONFLICT ... WHERE submitted_at IS NULL); archived
+  vacancies escaping the expiry sweep (OR archived_at IS NOT NULL).
+  **Semantic refinement 1 (metric honesty):** `resumed_at` is stamped on
+  the applicant's first post-resume SAVE (re-engagement), not on the resume
+  GET — mail-scanner prefetches would otherwise inflate the drafts-resumed
+  funnel (same reason erasure is GET-confirm + POST-delete). The resume
+  page carries the token in `data-resume-token`; the saver includes it in
+  the payload. The frozen I/O matrix's "resumed_at set once" still holds
+  (COALESCE); WHEN it sets moved from render to re-engagement.
+  **Semantic refinement 2 (email copy):** the shared requirements checklist
+  (invite/auto-reply/reminder-1/reminder-2) loses the one-visit rule for
+  the save-and-continue promise — the F3-SEAM seam's spirit applied to the
+  email half of the same claim.
+  KEEP: the debounced step-change save hook (F1's rt:form-step-changed),
+  the token-as-auth model, uniform-200/404 no-leak responses, the
+  strip-on-submit contract, and all pinned tests.
+  **Rejected:** two-tabs-stale-beacon overwrite (last-writer-wins is
+  acceptable at this scale; revision timestamps are over-engineering).
